<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-AFRICAN CLUB COMPETITION RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of first round, first leg matches in African club soccer competitions:</p>
<p>Played Saturday:</p>
<p>Conferation of African Football (CAF) Cup</p>
<p>In Tunis: Esperance (Tunisia) 7 Asko Kara (Togo) 0 (halftime 3-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Khaled Badra 5, Ayadi Hamrouni 6, 38, Faycal Ben Ahmed 57, 88, Sami Laroussi 77, Ryadh Jaidi 84</p>
<p>Attendance: 25,000  </p>
<p>Cup Winners' Cup</p>
<p>In Rabat: Royal Armed Forces (Morocco) 4 Real Bamako (Mali) 1 (2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Royal Armed Forces - Boucine Ouchella 23 pen, Mohamed Foulouh 35, Adil Tigradi 50, Ahderahim Rmouki 80</p>
<p>Real Bamako - Diallo Seko 85</p>
<p>Attendance - 4,000  </p>
<p>Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Curepipe, Mauritius: Sunrise Flacq United (Mauritius) 1 St Pierroise (Reunion) 0 (0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Fidy Rasoanaivo 87</p>
<p>Attendance: 7,000  </p>
<p>Played Sunday:</p>
<p>Champions' Cup</p>
<p>In Nairobi: Kenya Breweries (Kenya) 0 El Hilal (Sudan) 0</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,000  </p>
<p>CAF Cup:</p>
<p>In Dar es Salaam: Simba SC (Tanzania) 1 AFC Leopards (Kenya) 1 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Simba SC - George Lucas 69</p>
<p>AFC Leopards - Fred Ambare 6</p>
<p>Attendance: 14,000</p>
</text>
